## Completion checklist

M4 can be called complete only after luna can answer yes to all of these:

- VPCS/IOL bidirectional traffic was the first real hardware criterion and
  passed independently of commit `9916fb9`'s assertions.
- Multi-link and capture passed before the soak clock began.
- The soak ran at least 7,200 monotonic seconds, capture advanced throughout,
  and NAT/extnet work did not interrupt it.
- NAT outbound traffic and zero-residue teardown were measured.
- extnet was either executed with traffic/cleanup or explicitly recorded as
  not exercisable with raw Lima/interface/capability evidence.
- Four simultaneous 1024 MB IOL nodes passed, or the exact 8 GB hard wall was
  preserved and escalated without reducing scope.
- Forced launcher and forced VM termination each recovered with exactly zero
  stale fixture-owned processes/taps/bridges/rules before a successful recovery
  lab.
